{
  "an4.111:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.111 ",
  "an4.111:0.2": "12. With Kesi ",
  "an4.111:0.3": "With Kesi ",
  "an4.111:1.1": "Then Kesi the horse trainer went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to him, ",
  "an4.111:1.2": "“Kesi, you’re known as a horse trainer. ",
  "an4.111:1.3": "Just how do you guide a horse in training?” ",
  "an4.111:1.4": "“Sir, I guide a horse in training sometimes gently, sometimes harshly, and sometimes both gently and harshly.” ",
  "an4.111:1.5": "“Kesi, what do you do with a horse in training that doesn’t follow these forms of training?” ",
  "an4.111:1.6": "",
  "an4.111:1.7": "“In that case, sir, I kill it. ",
  "an4.111:1.8": "Why is that? ",
  "an4.111:1.9": "So that I don’t disgrace my tutor’s community. ",
  "an4.111:2.1": "But sir, the Buddha is the supreme guide for those fit for training. ",
  "an4.111:2.2": "Just how do you guide a person in training?” ",
  "an4.111:2.3": "“Kesi, I guide a person in training sometimes gently, sometimes harshly, and sometimes both gently and harshly. ",
  "an4.111:2.4": "The gentle way is this: ",
  "an4.111:2.5": "‘This is good conduct by way of body, speech, and mind. This is the result of good conduct by way of body, speech, and mind. This is life as a god. This is life as a human.’ ",
  "an4.111:2.6": "The harsh way is this: ",
  "an4.111:2.7": "‘This is bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind. This is the result of bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind.